        "thinking": "For F-10, the issue is that when `res._reject(e)` is called after the response is already settled (i.e., `_settled = true`), the error is silently dropped. Looking at the `_reject` method:\n\n```typescript\n_reject(e: unknown) { if (!this._settled) { this._settled = true; _rejectInner(e); } },\n```\n\nSo if `_settled` is already true (response already sent), the error just vanishes. And in `advance()`:\n\n\n```typescript\n.catch((e: unknown) =\u003e res._reject(e));\n```\n\nIf a handler throws after it already sent a response, the error gets dropped. The fix is to add logging for post-settled errors in both the `_reject` method and the catch handler in `advance()`.\n\nAdding error logging...",
        "type": "thinking"
